  "short_description": "550 Wp Vikram Solar Paradea bifacial glass-glass Mono PERC module, 21.29% efficient, IS 14286 certified, 45 mm hail tested, 30-year power warranty.",
  "long_description": "## What it is\n\nThe Vikram Solar Paradea VSMDH.72.550.05 is a 550 Wp bifacial glass-glass module built from 72 Mono PERC P-type bifacial cells cut into 144 half-cells on the M10 format and joined with multi-busbar ribbons. Both faces are glass — 2.0 mm anti-reflective coated semi-tempered low-iron glass in front, 2.0 mm heat-strengthened low-iron glass behind — laminated with an EVA/EPE encapsulant inside an anodised aluminium frame of twin-wall section. Module efficiency at standard test conditions is 21.29%.\n\n## What it's for\n\nCommercial and industrial rooftops, institutional campuses and ground-mounted plants, including single-axis trackers — the frame carries dedicated tracker holes as well as installing and grounding holes. A DCR-content version of this model is offered, which matters for subsidy-linked rooftop work in Andhra Pradesh and Telangana.\n\n## Key specifications\n\nAt STC the module delivers 550 Wp at 41.9 V and 13.14 A, with 49.7 V open-circuit and 13.82 A short-circuit, at a power tolerance of 0 to +3%. Temperature coefficients are −0.35 %/°C on power and −0.27 %/°C on Voc, NOCT is 45 °C ± 2 °C and the operating range is −40 °C to +85 °C. Maximum system voltage is 1500 V with a 25 A maximum series fuse. The laminate is rated for 5400 Pa of snow load and 2400 Pa of wind load and has passed a 45 mm hail test at impact velocities up to 27 m/s at a third-party laboratory. It measures 2278 mm × 1134 mm × 30 mm and weighs 32.5 kg. The IP68 split junction box carries individual bypass diodes and MC4-compatible leads. Certification covers IS 14286:2010 / IEC 61215:2005 and IS/IEC 61730 Parts 1 and 2, plus IEC 61701 salt mist, IEC 62716 ammonia and IEC 60068-2-68 sand and dust.\n\n## Application and installation notes\n\nFix it through the eight 9 × 14 mm installing holes; four Ø4 mm grounding holes and four 7 × 10 mm tracker holes are provided in the frame. Earth every module at a grounding hole. Being bifacial, it wants clearance and a reflective surface behind the array. Check string length against the 1500 V limit and the 49.7 V open-circuit voltage. At 32.5 kg it is a two-person lift.\n\n## What's in the box\n\nOne 550 Wp module with split junction box, cables and MC4-compatible connectors fitted. Structure, clamps, earthing hardware and DC cable are supplied separately; modules ship 36 to a pallet. Warranty: 12 years on product, 30 years linear on power, with 2% first-year degradation and 0.5% a year thereafter, reaching 83.5% of rated power at year 30.",
